<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Amalinde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Amalinde was fought in 1818 in what is now the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, between rival Xhosa forces. Warriors of the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndlambe">Ndlambe</a>, joined by Hintsa's Gcaleka, defeated his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngqika">Ngqika</a>, who then sought help from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>. The British intervention that followed led to the frontier war of 1818–1819.</p></div>
